{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition","id":1065949,"title":"Infernals - To Rule in Hell (complete edition)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Infernal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-03-21T14:48:27-07:00","id":1065949,"title":"Infernals - To Rule in Hell (complete edition)","content":"<a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zcIq5vae2GDx0AdkMkEDRY_1XAjSV6sEy6vWxpqqHdU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Link</a><br /> <br /> Some may remember this from a while back, it's now in a fully playable first draft state, with a total of 415 Infernal charms. It uses an ability-based charmset inspired by but not directly derived from the five Reclamation Yozis. There's still a fair amount that needs to be added, with some abilities and Shintais being seriously anemic compared to others, but there's enough to play a game with.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":3559,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","user":"Lanaya","date":". 09-24-2018, 09:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":19}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-21T15:24:11-07:00","id":1065978,"title":"","content":"This looks pretty awesome! Thanks for putting in the effort.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my RPG podcast: <a href=\"http://thestorytold.libsyn.com\" target=\"_blank\">The Story Told</a><br /> Follow my ongoing Exalted Campaign: <a href=\"https://thefallofjiara.obsidianportal.com/adventure-log\" target=\"_blank\">The Fall of Jiara</a><br /> Check out my Community Content: <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?author=Chazz%20Kellner\" target=\"_blank\">https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse....hazz%20Kellner</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/702-elfspeaker","name":"ElfSpeaker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar702_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"306"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-22T06:28:37-07:00","id":1066273,"title":"","content":"Any ideas of what to do with/for anima abilities?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-23T18:32:23-07:00","id":1067282,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1066273#post1066273\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any ideas of what to do with/for anima abilities?</div> </div> </div> </div>Shintais ate them for the most part. I'd like to add some small, flavourful anima abilities at some point if I can come up with good ones, but they'd very much be minor quirks that wouldn't change how your character plays very much. As a temporary kludge you could take a single anima ability from the corresponding Solar caste (I'd suggest diplomatic immunity for Fiends because oathbinding is disproportionately powerful, but it won't break anything either way).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-25T22:48:32-07:00","id":1068192,"title":"","content":"Oh hey I remember this. I unfortunately got too busy for a thorough read last time but I'm very hopeful to get a chance to give this a proper once-over, I remember seeing some good/cool stuff in there","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/655-senara","name":"Senara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar655_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T07:37:59-07:00","id":1068286,"title":"","content":"This is pretty interesting! I'm actually kludging the base Solar google sheet I use to work for this (mostly it involves renaming things and making things green).<br /> I definitely think that listing each Charm's associated Shintai in the Charm writeup is a good idea, if only to remove the need to flip back and forth between sections.<br /> <br /> Flicking through the charms, they seem nicely concise and flavorful---I'm not even done with Archery but I really like how some basically reward you for being a big bully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8026,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","user":"Beans","date":". 03-26-2017, 10:54 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T12:50:10-07:00","id":1068381,"title":"","content":"I'm torn. On the one hand, a workable Infernals fansplat! I'd bet significant money that there won't ever be another official Infernals book published, so having an option to use this for either PCs or villains is a big positive.<br /> <br /> On the other hand, stripping out the Yozi based Charmsets for an ability base makes Infernals lose a lot of their flavor. They're a lot closer to lime flavored Solars than they were in 2E. I'm aware that this is the current plan for the official Infernals as well, but that doesn't mean I have to like it.<br /> <br /> Still, from my somewhat informed opinion (I still don't have a huge experience base with 3E), it does look like a good Charmset and it's obvious that a lot a lot a lot of work went into it, so great job getting a finalized thing out!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2433-highpriest","name":"HighPriest","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2433_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T14:37:19-07:00","id":1068420,"title":"","content":"So a couple <i>really far off</i> questions. As in, it's cool you don't have an answer, but I'm curious (bc I love this homebrew and am using it for some future villians the Circle will encounter):<br /> Is Infernal Lore going to ever delve into the sort of catclysm stuff Solar Lore does? Like Dogstar Shrike or Wyld Shaping?<br /> Does the Survival charm that let's me wrestle a familar into being mine work on Demons?<br /> Do Infernals get Mastery Effects?<br /> Are you planning on custom merits for Infernals?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-26T16:25:22-07:00","id":1068461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1068420#post1068420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is Infernal Lore going to ever delve into the sort of catclysm stuff Solar Lore does? Like Dogstar Shrike or Wyld Shaping?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but only if I can come up with an interesting and clearly differentiated direction to take it in (or if someone else does, I'm always happy to take charm suggestions). Shrike in particular is on my list of iconic/awesome Solar charms that would make for excellent and thematically appropriate Infernal charms but which I'm deliberately not giving Infernals a version of because I prefer them to remain Solar charms. I could justify looting pretty much every cool thing Solars get for Infernals and giving them Infernal charms on top of that, but that's not a direction I'm a fan of. That said, it's an aggregate thing; there's no one Solar charm that cannot be ported without causing damage to the definition of Solars and Infernals, so if you want to give equivalents to your villains that'd be perfectly reasonable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1068420#post1068420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Does the Survival charm that let's me wrestle a familar into being mine work on Demons?</div> </div> </div> </div>It certainly should and I've added that in, though they won't benefit at all from a lot of the later familiar-boosting charms. I might write up a mini-tree specifically for demon familiars later, or add on alternate effects to the charms that don't benefit them.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1068420#post1068420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do Infernals get Mastery Effects?</div> </div> </div> </div>They do.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1068420#post1068420\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Are you planning on custom merits for Infernals?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not opposed to it, but I also don't see any of the backgrounds in MoEP: Infernals as needing to be ported over. Demonic familiars are just demonic familiars, savant and unwoven coadjutor are easily modelled by taking appropriate dots and specialties, spies is just contacts and past life is... interesting but something I'd prefer as taking appropriate dots and specialties and roleplaying the rest in whatever ways seem appropriate to your character.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T10:41:46-07:00","id":1068743,"title":"","content":"How much would you say your Infernal model leans (or doesn't lean) toward the Infernal preview thematically, with the whole &quot;GSPs are reflections of First Age Solars at their most vice-steeped and excess-driven&quot; thing they have goin' on? I've been sort of looking toward that and perhaps toward some aspects of 2.5e Infernals in that both my Infernal characters' concepts involve their lives going down the shitter and them basically saying &quot;this can't be happening to me, it's not fair,&quot; and the Yozis latching onto that despair and frustration to say &quot;Yeah, you're owed so much better... how about we give you the power to take what life owes you?&quot;<br /> Admittedly I'm just shuffling this together after seeing this homebrew yesterday morning, so I could be way off the mark (if there is indeed a mark for me to be off of).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8026-beans","name":"Beans","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8026_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"472"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T13:59:09-07:00","id":1068864,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Beans</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1068743#post1068743\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How much would you say your Infernal model leans (or doesn't lean) toward the Infernal preview thematically, with the whole &quot;GSPs are reflections of First Age Solars at their most vice-steeped and excess-driven&quot; thing they have goin' on?</div> </div> </div> </div>I really like that concept, but it's not particularly represented in the charmset. Which certainly isn't to say that you can't do it, just that the rules won't be guiding you in that direction. The character concepts you mentioned do sound pretty much exactly like the kinds of Infernals I'd be making though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-03-27T18:20:09-07:00","id":1068964,"title":"","content":"Made some minor fixes, including adding certain dodge and shintai-boosting charms that had disappeared at some point, and as some had requested I've added the Shintai associated with each Shintai charm on its requirements line. I also split everything into separate docs by ability, since the megadoc was getting too laggy to manage.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T15:59:38-07:00","id":1071833,"title":"","content":"Might I suggest an infernal Occult charm (under Ceclenye maybe? OR maybe it'd be survival?) that allows for the creation of a custom demon? I think 2e infernals could do this, and demon's are different enough from elementals/invited Raksha to seperate it from the Solar charm.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-01T23:44:09-07:00","id":1071941,"title":"","content":"So I like the quality and direction overall- not what I would have done but certainly better than I could have managed, and I always love seeing an alternate take.<br /> <br /> My only quibble, from what I'm seeing here, is that due to the singular focus on a given Yozi for a given Ability, certain pieces appear to be missing- for instance, any mention of Feats of Strength in athletics, even though being massively strong could be a very deeply appropriate thing for a mighty Malfean type or what have you.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/655-senara","name":"Senara","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar655_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"73"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-02T01:33:38-07:00","id":1071955,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epee102</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1071833#post1071833\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Might I suggest an infernal Occult charm (under Ceclenye maybe? OR maybe it'd be survival?) that allows for the creation of a custom demon? I think 2e infernals could do this, and demon's are different enough from elementals/invited Raksha to seperate it from the Solar charm.</div> </div> </div> </div>There kind of is in the form of the medicine charm that lets you make a creature of your choice, but to give some variety in your demon-spawning I added back the ability for From Desolation, Life to create a new breed of demon of your own design. Can't quite remember why I got rid of that effect in the first place, actually.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Senara</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1071941#post1071941\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My only quibble, from what I'm seeing here, is that due to the singular focus on a given Yozi for a given Ability, certain pieces appear to be missing- for instance, any mention of Feats of Strength in athletics, even though being massively strong could be a very deeply appropriate thing for a mighty Malfean type or what have you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah, yeah. I've been meaning to write a Malfean feat of strength tree for ages, but I've struggled with finding a way to do it that's not just the Solar tree with more sinister names, and unlike the Solar craft charms I copied over I feel like I should be able to come up with something compelling and unique. Just hasn't quite come to me yet.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:38:18-07:00","id":1073115,"title":"","content":"Hey Lanaya! I was actually looking to make some Infernal antagonists for my players and so I found this homebrew and I freaking love it! It's just so fun to create an infernal with this homebrew <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> Great job!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12044-chaosarchon","name":"ChaosArchon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12044_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"82"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-05-30T16:40:00-07:00","id":1098607,"title":"","content":"We are using this fan-splat in our group and loving it. The pirate-king Demon Emperor Shintai Fiend Caste is just AWESOME","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T15:48:34-07:00","id":1099313,"title":"","content":"Small update, I've finally figured out a way of doing feat of strength charms that I liked. Here they are.<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>False Idols Cast Down</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m;<b> Mins: </b>Athletics 3, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> Surging with fell might, the Infernal adds her Essence to her Strength score for the purpose of qualifying for a feat of strength, and gains (Essence) non-Charm dice on the roll. If she attempts to destroy an object while one or more other characters who bear positive Ties towards it can witness the destruction she wreaks, the difficulty of the feat of strength is reduced by the intensity of the strongest such Intimacy, reducing the Strength requirement appropriately.<br /> <br /> <b>Tower-Toppling Fist</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Athletics 4, Essence 2 <i>(The King Still Stands)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>False Idols Cast Down<br /> With this Charm the Infernal can perform feats of strength to destroy objects at a greatly accelerated pace. A destructive feat that would take a day is instead completed in an hour, one that would take an hour takes a minute, one that would take a minute takes one action and one that would take an action becomes reflexive. At Essence 3+, the Infernal can reduce the time required to perform a feat by two stages.<br /> <br /> <b>Growing Frenzy Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Athletics 5, Essence 3 <i>(The King Still Stands)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>False Idols Cast Down<br /> Each act of destruction only spurs the Infernal on to another. She gains (Strength) bonus dice and two non-Charm bonus dice on a feat of strength roll, plus two additional non-Charm dice for each time she has successfully used this Charm in the current scene, to a maximum of (Strength + Essence) dice.<br /> <br /> <b>World-Crushing Solace</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-;<b> Mins: </b>Athletics 5, Essence 3 <i>(The King Still Stands)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Growing Frenzy Attitude<br /> Once per scene when the Infernal succeeds on a feat of strength to destroy something with a difficulty equal to at least (5 + her Essence), she regains one point of Willpower.<br /> <br /> <b>City-Smiting Ruin</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>12m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Athletics 5, Essence 5 <i>(The King Still Stands)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>World-Crushing Solace<br /> The Infernal\u2019s power is endless and untiring. Nothing can stand in the face of her rampage. She doubles 7s on feat of strength rolls, and can attempt any feat regardless of Strength requirement.</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-01T15:52:33-07:00","id":1099315,"title":"","content":"One question, I have the pdf you released in March, with 170 pages. What is the difference with the bunch of pdfs in your main page? There are too many to manually download and see the differences one by one. Were too many charms added? In which abilities? To see if it is worth to download one by one and send to my player...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-03T17:44:39-07:00","id":1099964,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Clophiroth</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1099315#post1099315\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One question, I have the pdf you released in March, with 170 pages. What is the difference with the bunch of pdfs in your main page? There are too many to manually download and see the differences one by one. Were too many charms added? In which abilities? To see if it is worth to download one by one and send to my player...</div> </div> </div> </div>There wasn't a pdf, but if you mean the google docs, I <i>think</i> the only changes I've made since then are adding the feat of strength charms and noting in each charm's prereqs line which Shintai it's associated with. I might be wrong on that, but either way there weren't any major revisions.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-04T00:50:07-07:00","id":1100038,"title":"","content":"Yes, I meant the Google Doc. I usualy download these Docs as PDFs, as I find them easier to read than Word/Open Office documents, so forgot it never was a PDF to start with XD<br /> <br /> A doubt with Black Mirror Shintai, mostly related to Charms. As you &quot;replace your Charms with the target\u00b4s&quot;<br /> <br /> 1): If the target is non-Exalted, non-God, non-magical creature, so, a mortal person... As you replaced your Charms with his/hers, that is, nothing, I guess you lose access to Charms until you come back to your real form?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13031-clophiroth","name":"Clophiroth","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13031_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T11:18:24-07:00","id":1100514,"title":"","content":"Is this material complete, no additional content to be added or revised?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-06-05T13:41:16-07:00","id":1100559,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Maudova</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1100514#post1100514\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Is this material complete, no additional content to be added or revised?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's complete in the sense that there's enough here to play with, but there is more content that I plan to add.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-08T22:29:30-08:00","id":1157197,"title":"","content":"Minor update to show I haven't totally forgotten about this. I fleshed out presence and thrown a bit, including an Act of Villainy charm for those who were fond of that mechanic. Here's the new stuff:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\"><b>Dastardly Villain Attitude</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-;<b> Mins: </b>Presence 2, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>None<br /> An Infernal with this Charm derives no end of satisfaction from acting the role of the worst kind of monster. Upon purchasing Dastardly Villain Attitude, she picks two of the following acts of villainy. When she meets the condition for one of her chosen acts, she gains a point of Willpower and can lose one point of Limit, though she can only perform each given act once per story. Additional acts can be bought for 3xp each.<br /> <b>Infernal Genius Declaration: </b>The Infernal shares the details of her master plan with her enemies, knowing that they will be able to use this information against her and potentially thwart that plan.<br /> <b>Best Enemy Recognition: </b>After developing a positive Tie towards an enemy who poses some threat to her, the Infernal assists him at no benefit to herself or spares him when he is wholly in her power.<br /> <b>Fiendish Deathtrap Compulsion: </b>Rather than personally deal with her enemies, the Infernal leaves them to be slain or held captive by her minions, a deadly environmental feature or some elaborate trap.<br /> <b>Trusted Companion Subversion: </b>Rather than oppose her foe directly, the Infernal deploys some scheme to turn the subject of one of his positive Ties against him.<br /> <b>Chivalrous Fiend Obligation: </b>The Infernal sacrifices some substantial advantage over a foe to give him a fighting chance, such as by ordering her troops to stand down so she can fight him one on one.<br /> <br /> <b>Wrapped in Adoration<br /> Cost: </b>5m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Presence 5, Essence 2 <i>(Black Mirror Shintai)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Cunning Deception Technique<br /> An Infernal with this Charm inspires deep and abiding passion in others \u2013 usually trust and devotion, but some delight in making others utterly consumed in hatred for themselves. When confronted with a character bearing a Defining Tie towards herself, the Infernal can roll a special (Manipulation + Presence) instill action to make that Tie inviolable. If she succeeds, any persuasion that would cause her target to act against the affected Tie can and must be treated as unacceptable influence.<br /> If the targeted Intimacy is lowered in strength, this Charm\u2019s effects end. However, any successful attempt made to reduce it must be rerolled, taking the second result instead.<br /> <br /> <b>Passion-Exploiting Artistry</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>-;<b> Mins: </b>Presence 5, Essence 2 <i>(Black Mirror Shintai)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>None<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Wrapped in Adoration<br /> An Infernal with this Charm never needs to roll to convince others to act on a Defining Tie towards herself. Furthermore, if she requests an inconvenient task, the target of her influence cannot attempt to resist in a Decision Point except when another character attempts to overturn the influence.<br /> <br /> <b>Armoured in Impropriety Approach<br /> Cost: </b>7m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Presence 5, Essence 3 <i>(Black Mirror Shintai)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Mute<br /> <b>Duration: </b>One scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Our Little Secret<br /> The Infernal\u2019s dark deeds are too confronting to even witness. Any character who sees her grossly violate social mores or laws will refuse to acknowledge her actions, instead continuing as though nothing had happened. Even after this Charm has ended, such characters will not remember that anything happened, having forced the incident out of their minds. The Infernal\u2019s act must be something unsettling, not merely unacceptable \u2013 she could murder a satrap in front of his court and walk out unchallenged, but stealing from his treasury would not be aided by this Charm.<br /> A character whose Major or Defining Intimacy that is threatened by the Infernal can spend a point of Willpower to ignore this Charm\u2019s effects.<br /> <br /> <b>Dust Devil Feint</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>3m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Thrown 5, Essence 1<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Sandstrike Blast<br /> As she flays her foes alive, the Infernal dissolves into grains of sand herself and reappears elsewhere. After the completion of a <b>withering </b>attack made with Sandstrike Blast, she can transport herself one range band in any direction as long as she doesn\u2019t move through a impermeable barrier.<br /> <br /> <b>A Thousand Grains<br /> Cost: </b>1m;<b> Mins: </b>Thrown 4, Essence 2 <i>(Shintai of the Endless Desert)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Uniform<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Flesh-Flensing Barrage<br /> Eventually even the most stubborn defence must wear away before the Infernal\u2019s persistent onslaught. An attack enhanced by this Charm gains no benefit itself; however, if the Infernal attacks the same target on her next turn (or before it using reflexive attack Charms) she rerolls all 6s on that attack roll. Each round that she uses this Charm consecutively against the same target she rerolls the next lowest number as well, to a maximum of (Essence) different rerolled numbers, so after three rounds the Infernal will reroll 6s, 5s and 4s. If the Infernal fails to activate this Charm against her target for a full round, all her accumulated rerolls are lost.<br /> <br /> <b>Pitiless Choking Wreath<br /> Cost: </b>4m;<b> Mins: </b>Thrown 3, Essence 2 <i>(Shintai of the Endless Desert)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Sandstrike Blast<br /> If the Infernal\u2019s <b>withering </b>attack using Sandstrike Blast is successful, her target is enfolded in her sands, which continue to scrape at his flesh. He suffers an additional point of <b>withering </b>damage at the beginning of each of his turns until he escapes. Escaping the sands requires an action and a successful (Dexterity + Athletics) roll against a difficulty of (Infernal\u2019s Thrown).<br /> If the Infernal\u2019s attack crashes her target, his airways are additionally flooded with sand and he begins to suffocate until he is freed.<br /> <br /> <b>Swallowed in Eternity</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>5m;<b> Mins: </b>Thrown 3, Essence 2 <i>(Shintai of the Endless Desert)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Pitiless Choking Wreath<br /> While she has an enemy trapped in the Pitiless Choking Wreath, the Infernal can make a special <b>decisive </b>gambit using Sandstrike Blast at a difficulty equal to the target\u2019s remaining health levels, which cannot be parried. If it succeeds, the ground beneath her target\u2019s feet dissolves into sand which drags him under, never to be seen again. Whatever fate awaits him is unknown, save that Exalted victims of this Charm may not reincarnate until several years later.<br /> <br /> <b>Death Races Onwards<br /> Cost: </b>6m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Thrown 5, Essence 3 <i>(Scarlet Rapture Shintai)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Decisive-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Carried on the Wind, Hungry Wind Howling<br /> After making a successful close range <b>decisive </b>attack, the Infernal launches herself two or three range bands forward and makes a secondary <b>decisive </b>attack applied against each other enemy she comes within close range of during this move. This attack carries a base damage of the Infernal\u2019s Essence plus any threshold successes on the attack roll, and does not reduce the Infernal\u2019s Initiative on a miss. Using this Charm counts as the Infernal\u2019s movement action for the round.<br /> <br /> <b>Scorpion-Tailed Mirage Technique</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>11m, 1wp;<b> Mins: </b>Thrown 5, Essence 3 <i>(Shintai of the Endless Desert)</i><br /> <b>Type: </b>Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords: </b>Perilous, Withering-only<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Dust Devil Feint, Dune-Burst Onslaught<br /> As her enemies try to strike her down, the Infernal explodes into a blast of sand that scrapes skin from their bones. She makes a reflexive <b>withering </b>clash against an incoming attack using her Sandstrike Blast, which automatically benefits from Dust Devil Feint.<br /> <br /> <b>Updated Charm: World-Grinding Sandstorm Devastation</b><br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Swallowed in Eternity, Scorpion-Tailed Mirage Technique</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T06:50:08-08:00","id":1157519,"title":"","content":"Gonna tip my hat to you on this one, that was a remarkable project that you have brought to the Exalted community. In our group, we are going with mixed types of Exalted, so can't wait to see the Infernals you have created in action.<br /> <br /> One thing our group was quick to notice that it seems Flesh-Flensing Barrage seems excessively strong when combo-ed with Crimson Storm Unleashed. Perhaps limiting it by (Essence) or (Thrown) stacks of penalty could add a balancing factor to the combo? That, and I would like to ask if Pitiless Choking Wreath is meant to be supplemental, since I was confused to see it referencing a withering attack by Sandstrike Blast, yet in itself the charm doesn't make that attack.<br /> <br /> Once again, thank you very much for your hardwork!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21512-buraikhoi","name":"Buraikhoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T08:24:25-08:00","id":1157546,"title":"","content":"Im putting this post in my bookmarks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11395-shaddar","name":"Shaddar","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"338"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-10T11:58:35-08:00","id":1157603,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Buraikhoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1157519#post1157519\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing our group was quick to notice that it seems Flesh-Flensing Barrage seems excessively strong when combo-ed with Crimson Storm Unleashed. Perhaps limiting it by (Essence) or (Thrown) stacks of penalty could add a balancing factor to the combo? That, and I would like to ask if Pitiless Choking Wreath is meant to be supplemental, since I was confused to see it referencing a withering attack by Sandstrike Blast, yet in itself the charm doesn't make that attack.</div> </div> </div> </div>Capped it to (Essence) stacks, thanks for that suggestion. Also cleared up Pitiless Choking Wreath's wording to make it clear that it includes the attack.<br /> <br /> And thanks for the kind words, to everyone who's given them! It means a lot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T05:14:03-08:00","id":1159385,"title":"","content":"Any chance this can be complied into a single document? Would make it so much easier for my group to look through...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T11:07:56-08:00","id":1159488,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>FallenEco</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1159385#post1159385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Any chance this can be complied into a single document? Would make it so much easier for my group to look through...</div> </div> </div> </div>It was originally a single doc, but at that size google docs started to lag horribly and I couldn't keep it updated so I had to switch to this setup. I made a quick compiled <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1uZj9UDSg4-isbi6XZGe6IYqPrJlcUFdb\" target=\"_blank\">pdf version</a> though, it's not pretty but it's searchable.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T13:45:13-08:00","id":1159546,"title":"","content":"That's a pretty nice homebrew while waiting for the official Infernals to come out. I remember reading about Adorjan and her charms, and immediately coming up with the concept of a boddhisattva-like Infernal preaching complete detachment from everything to both escape the cycle of reincarnation AND avoid the Neverborn's fate (no guarantee it's a viable philosophy, but hey, Exalted come up with that sort of ambitious projects all the time). An extreme, brutal kind of enlightenment and detachment that doesn't appear very nice for the average onlooker, but that's close to the most benevolent interpretation of Adorjan's influence (Yozi influence in general, even) I could come up with. I'm seeing many Essence 1 charms alone that'd be relevant for that concept, so that's encouraging. I might make her an NPC in my current game before I try playing her as a PC someday.<br /> (Also, this homebrew is making me realize that she'd actually also draw quite a lot from the Ebon Dragon, which is ironic but very interesting for a character who's meant to be &quot;good&quot;, or at least genuinely trying to...)<br /> Thanks for your work!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Part-time table flipper.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/519-chairkicker","name":"ChairKicker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar519_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"237"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-11-16T14:59:06-08:00","id":1159575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lanaya</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1159488#post1159488\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It was originally a single doc, but at that size google docs started to lag horribly and I couldn't keep it updated so I had to switch to this setup. I made a quick compiled <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/open?id=1uZj9UDSg4-isbi6XZGe6IYqPrJlcUFdb\" target=\"_blank\">pdf version</a> though, it's not pretty but it's searchable.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you! Great work","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Thoughts ripple out, birthing others","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1624-falleneco","name":"FallenEco","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1624_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1927"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T01:53:01-08:00","id":1170386,"title":"","content":"Previously, Crimson Storm Unleashed was meant to be a combo with Flesh-Flensing Barrage from the looks of the 2 charms. Now that FFB has been limited to 3 or Essence stacks, do you have any plan to revisit the former and perhaps tweak its mechanism a bit?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/21512-buraikhoi","name":"Buraikhoi","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"14"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-25T12:52:53-08:00","id":1170509,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Buraikhoi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1170386#post1170386\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Previously, Crimson Storm Unleashed was meant to be a combo with Flesh-Flensing Barrage from the looks of the 2 charms. Now that FFB has been limited to 3 or Essence stacks, do you have any plan to revisit the former and perhaps tweak its mechanism a bit?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good point. I removed the requirement to make all the attacks against the same target, so you can start flensing another target once you reach the cap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-26T18:32:06-08:00","id":1170825,"title":"","content":"For the most part, this is an amazing piece of homebrew, definitely hanging out with ACoD at the top of my &quot;could basically just use as canon&quot; list. The charms are flavorful, powerful, and intuitive and I'm beyond impressed by the sheer number you've made.<br /> <br /> I'm conflicted about how the Shintai's turned out, though. On the one hand, using Shintai's as a way to feed Supernalesque essence requirement waivers is a stroke of brilliance. It really delivers on a 2E feeling of being able to access charms based around a Yozi's theme while also retaining the intuitive balance and structure of ability charm trees. Also, tying it to Caste theoretically allows for infernals that embody different interpretations of each Yozi. That being said, I find that the actual execution is a little bit &quot;lumpy.&quot; I say that tying it to caste is theoretically a way to differentiate Shintais they mostly have ability spreads that favor one Caste so heavily that it is hard to imagine why you would take it with any other. For instance, there is almost no conceivable reason to take Scarlet Rapture or The King Still Stands if you aren't a Slayer because their spreads so heavily favor those two classes.<br /> <br /> I tried to think up some ways to fix it, but most of them come down to, &quot;Shintais need more and varied charms attached to them&quot; and that is a big ask on a project already as big as this. The other way I think this would be fixable would be to actually narrow up some of the Shintais and create some additional ones.<br /> <br /> Lastly on Shintais, I have a love-hate relationship with the activation conditions. Some of them are truly brilliant for both flavor and gameplay balance. Heuristic Logos, for instance, is amazing. It is so evocative of a particular type of character and it sets up so many &quot;Just according to keikaku&quot; moments. Both Black Mirror and Tenebrous Apotheosis have similarly reasonable to meet and flavorful activation conditions. Then there are ones like Scarlet Rapture which just seems insane. In a certain type of campaign, I could see this getting a lot of activation, but if you are doing one which doesn't typically feature Size 5 battlegroups or similar, the activation probably won't come up. I guess, musing about activation conditions, the best ones are built around how you play the game and manuevering your character and their enemies into position to demon-out and crush your foes while the weaker ones seem to amount to &quot;did you buy Command/Cult 3+ or does your GM like big battlegroups and they cannot lie.&quot;<br /> <br /> All in all, though, I agree with your statement that this is completely playable and I look forward to seeing what you add and change.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-27T23:28:07-08:00","id":1171158,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1170825#post1170825\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">On the one hand, using Shintai's as a way to feed Supernalesque essence requirement waivers is a stroke of brilliance. It really delivers on a 2E feeling of being able to access charms based around a Yozi's theme while also retaining the intuitive balance and structure of ability charm trees.</div> </div> </div> </div>Really happy to read this; it's exactly what I was trying to do with the shintai system. As for the rest, they're definitely issues that I've been struggling to find good solutions for. Shintai activation triggers are a particularly thorny one since it seems everyone I talk to has different ideas about which ones are reasonably achievable and which ones are too impractical to work. Probably does just come down to individual player/ST styles.<br /> <br /> In regards to charm distributions, my current solution is indeed to write more charms that give each shintai more varied things to do across castes. It's slow going because at this point all the charms that quickly and intuitively spring to mind for me are charms I've already written up, but fleshing out the more narrow trees and shintais is what I'm currently working on so I hope to get some done in the future.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-28T12:50:11-08:00","id":1171308,"title":"","content":"I think that part of the issue with activation triggers is that, by the end of 2E, Shintais were all over the place in terms of power and function. Some were apocalyptic transformations, some were minor, Kamen Rider transformations, some were literally just normal attacks with weird fluff; ultimately, this just means there are people walking around with different wants from their Shintais. For transparency's sake, I like a combo of Kamen Rider transformations and big, radical transhumanism transformations. This is bad luck because the approach that you are taking to Shintais is that they're mutually exclusive and all about as powerful as each other. Which basically means that whichever you go for, somebody will find it disappointing. Such is life, though, right?<br /> <br /> I guess the easy way out is to provide multiple conditions for activation. Maybe offering a choice of conditions at character creation so players and storytellers can work together to make sure that this fairly Splat defining feature sees use. It might also be worth investigating giving each Caste a Shintai activation option that could pop up in response to caste specific setbacks and difficulties. The nuclear option is just letting people pay motes and willpower (10m, 1-2wp, I would guess), but that is boring compared to the flavorful options there now.<br /> <br /> If you are up for a slightly more radical redesign, could also make Shintai effects more Caste-Power-like by giving them three effects, a weak always on thing, possibly no better than a control spell ish effect, a reasonably strong power with an activation condition that is basically impossible not to hit when using powers within the Shintai's themes, and a big, show stopper effect which takes lots of effort to activate and could not even come up depending on the campaign. Again, that might be a big ask and could bloat the Shintai's so, <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:16px\">\u00af\\_(\u30c4)_/\u00af</span></span></span><br /> <br /> Also, if you are having some trouble coming up with charms, I highly suggest adding in more Yozis for charms to align with. Adding new thematics could give you some more creative juice and, since 3E is trying to expand the scope of hell to not be about the five titanic douchebags plotting a prison break, more yozis is a good way to broaden the scope of hell. Also, if you would like some inspirational material, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/pub?id=1jmxwx7FPXA-jzWJiv2fyCGeJQGQu2QomFTs5j45mPec#h.npx320douya7\" target=\"_blank\">Earth Scorpion's Homebrew</a> has some pretty robust charm sets which could be decent jumping off points for making Szoreny, Kimbrey, and Oramus charms. Also, bits of the homebrew contain links to documents for Isidoros and Hegera charm sets too. It's very much of a 2E transhumanist- titanomachia design paradigm, but so were a lot of the canon 2E charms and you did a great job adapting those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Exalted is an aesthetic.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5526-steamfunk","name":"Steamfunk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5526_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"222"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-01-17T12:58:24-08:00","id":1176823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Steamfunk</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1171308#post1171308\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Also, if you are having some trouble coming up with charms, I highly suggest adding in more Yozis for charms to align with. Adding new thematics could give you some more creative juice and, since 3E is trying to expand the scope of hell to not be about the five titanic douchebags plotting a prison break, more yozis is a good way to broaden the scope of hell. Also, if you would like some inspirational material, <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/pub?id=1jmxwx7FPXA-jzWJiv2fyCGeJQGQu2QomFTs5j45mPec#h.npx320douya7\" target=\"_blank\">Earth Scorpion's Homebrew</a> has some pretty robust charm sets which could be decent jumping off points for making Szoreny, Kimbrey, and Oramus charms. Also, bits of the homebrew contain links to documents for Isidoros and Hegera charm sets too. It's very much of a 2E transhumanist- titanomachia design paradigm, but so were a lot of the canon 2E charms and you did a great job adapting those.</div> </div> </div> </div>At the very least, I think Kimbery could be added for some not-Malfeas Sail charms (although given Malfeas has the enviromental hazard generation already, that might not be needed). Given Kimbery was kinda the 6th ranger of the Reclamation, adding her in might be an intreasitng place to go.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>The Book of Laughing Serpents Series(Latest <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/293793/Book-of-Laughing-Serpents-Volume-7\" target=\"_blank\">Here</a>)<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/287741/Many-Limbed-Manual?src=hottest_filtered&amp;filters=45622\" target=\"_blank\">Many Limbed Manual</a><br /> Patreon here: <a href=\"https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety\" target=\"_blank\">https://patreon.com/undeadauthorsociety</a><br /> San Jeanro Co-Op writer. Volume 1 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/278871/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 2 <a href=\"https://t.co/SXRLElZlw4?amp=1\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> Volume 3 <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/297692/The-Short-Games-Digest-Volume-3?affiliate_id=389642\" target=\"_blank\">here</a><br /> My folklore and horror blog, here:<a href=\"http://undeadauthorsociety.wordpres.com/\" target=\"_blank\">http://undeadauthorsociety.com</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11835-epee102","name":"Epee102","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11835_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2102"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T02:50:27-07:00","id":1255690,"title":"","content":"I like your work. I'm a bit concerned about the activation conditions of some of the shintais. Black Mirror Shintai requiring a defining negative tie seems harsh. It might have to do with different playstyles, but having/cultivating a defining ties with an npc seems like a once per campaign type of effect to me. Am I missing something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13122-mordekain","name":"Mordekain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-20T12:32:07-07:00","id":1255833,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Mordekain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1255690#post1255690\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like your work. I'm a bit concerned about the activation conditions of some of the shintais. Black Mirror Shintai requiring a defining negative tie seems harsh. It might have to do with different playstyles, but having/cultivating a defining ties with an npc seems like a once per campaign type of effect to me. Am I missing something?</div> </div> </div> </div>Iiiiiiit probably is too harsh? But it's a powerful effect to be able to throw out, and it's the easiest kind of defining to create since making people hate you is a lot easier to do than making them love you. Ultimately the problem is I have no idea whether it's too harsh or not, it's the kind of thing that's almost impossible to figure out just by thinking about it and I'm never going to have groups of playtesters large enough to give statistically useful feedback all trying to use Black Mirror in game and reporting on how practical it is. My advice would be that if you're using these rules and are finding it too difficult to trigger, drop the requirement down to major and see how that works out for you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3559-lanaya","name":"Lanaya","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3559_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"960"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-21T07:03:26-07:00","id":1256092,"title":"","content":"Of course... but the thing is, that building negative intimacies to a defining level against yourself also seems a bit obvious. My suggestion would be to allow activation when confronted by someone with a defining intimacy that is antithetical to one of your own defining intimacies. That way it is more about the meeting of opposite beliefs and less about making your enemies hate you. I don't really know if that will make activation easier though. As you said it can be pretty much impossible to figure out by thought alone.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13122-mordekain","name":"Mordekain","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"23"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T09:00:58-07:00","id":1256968,"title":"","content":"I see you didn't include Running To Forever's 2nd Purchase (the one that generalized the ability). <br /> Couldn't find the right place to put it? <br /> <br /> Also is this compiled into a master document or would I need to do so manually?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4983-graywalker","name":"GrayWalker","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4983_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"157"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-09-24T18:16:43-07:00","id":1257059,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>GrayWalker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/infernal-exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition?p=1256968#post1256968\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I see you didn't include Running To Forever's 2nd Purchase (the one that generalized the ability).<br /> Couldn't find the right place to put it?<br /> <br /> Also is this compiled into a master document or would I need to do so manually?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's been a long time since I wrote the athletics charms, I don't remember much about my thought process at the time. Seems like a fine effect to include as a repurchase if you'd like to use it though.<br /> <br /> I initially broke it up into mini documents because my computer couldn't handle viewing a full-sized one, let one editing it. I've upgraded since though, so here's a <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1zcIq5vae2GDx0AdkMkEDRY_1XAjSV6sEy6vWxpqqHdU/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">master document</a> for you.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">My homebrew: <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1244979-abyssals-a-shadow-falls\" target=\"_blank\">Abyssals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1065949-infernals-to-rule-in-hell-complete-edition\" target=\"_blank\">Infernals,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/781489-ex3-dragon-kings-homebrew\" target=\"_blank\">Dragon Kings,</a> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1058142-lanaya-s-martial-arts-homebrew-compendium\" target=\"_blank\">martial arts.</a></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":""